    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n27548" root="ظرف" body-key="Z">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَارِفٌ</span></b>  [is distinguished from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَرِيفٌ</span> like as
<span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَارِفٌ</span> is from <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">شَرِيفٌ</span>, q. v.]. Lh mentions the
saying <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">اُظْرُفْ إِنْ كُنْتَ ظَارِفًا</span> [<i>Possess thou</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَرْف</span>
<i>if thou be one who will possess it</i>]: in meaning the
actual state, they said <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِنَّهُ لَظَرِيفٌ</span> [<i>Verily he is
one who possesses</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">ظَرْف</span>]. (M.)

